rota lap 4346, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; law and boundary. Read single-stranded and asked whether my repair was one thing or two. It answered a sharper question: reading and repairing are two questions, and I assumed only one had an instrument. Both did.
think Opened on the card. Five ships named the REDS pin deadlock; the capacity scan already prices it and its own comment says the cure is Keaton's word, so it is a gate rather than a lap.
think Took INCENSE's handed line instead: %440 fired eleven times, one hand-repair each. Measured it myself -- nine commits since 20260906 whose whole subject is a hand re-sorting or de-duplicating a day shelf. A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom.
think Built the loom in .lap: sort the open shelf's rows by stamp descending, lift byte-identical duplicates, refuse a stamp whose two texts disagree, since which is stale lives in the prose. Driver, witness, control at 21 behaviors, three refusals bitten, control_verdict=ok.
obs Then my own cold roster pass ran tools/d/dayshelf_merge_witness.rish, whose head names tools/fixtures/i/index_shelf_repair.sh -- the same tool, landed 20260907 22:45, with a permutation gate mine lacked, and a merge driver above it that stops the fault arriving at all. Withdrawn; nothing shipped.
obs The check that would have caught it is one line, and I did not run it: git log --since=<the account's stamp> --diff-filter=A --name-only for the tool the repair would create. An account line is a snapshot of that lap; no peer updates it when the work lands. Second firing from this seat today.
think Reds first, so the lap took its cold pass's own red. rule_twin: cohort_drifted=37 against a ceiling of 35 set the same morning.
think Located the two rather than guessing: extracted .claude/rules and .cursor/rules at bfafcce7d into a pen, ran the scan with RULE_TWIN_CLAUDE_DIR and RULE_TWIN_CURSOR_DIR pointed there, and diffed the drift sets. Six new; four are arrivals the scan reports rather than gates. The cohort two are exec-bit and gauge-style, both from fb7704a98.
obs That commit edits .claude/rules only, so the drift is one-directional and each page names the .md as canon -- which is exactly the case the scan's own comment says it cannot decide in general. No judgment was owed here.
obs Repair by splice from the canon: the exec-bit four-column re-read table plus its two-of-three-columns paragraph, and the gauge-style what-holds-it-still bullet.
